# UI interaction guidelines

When changing UI, navigation, forms, modals, tables, preferences, import/learning flows, password handling, security-sensitive code, or project documentation, follow:

**[docs/ui-interaction-guidelines.md](docs/ui-interaction-guidelines.md)**

That playbook is the source of truth for:

1. Simplified UI menus (short top bar; admin under profile; mobile hubs)
2. Tables: filtering + per-user customizability where browse density warrants it
3. Action button placement (secondary left, primary/proceed right)
4. Visual clarity (contrast, spacing, in-field controls)
5. Viewport-safe centered modals
6. View continuity (preferences merge, URL filters, scroll restore)
7. System learning (mapping recall, rename/merge aliases) — no speculative ML
8. Password handling basics
9. AI coding security don’ts (defensive checklist)
10. Required documentation set outlines

Prefer stack-agnostic habits from the playbook; use “In this project…” callouts for Laravel/Blade/Alpine specifics. Do not invent new learning systems or retrofit column pickers onto every admin index unless the playbook (or an explicit request) requires it.
